# Why each tag below does not apply. Detail: docs/design/packaging.md, "Lintian".

# cargo-deb 2.12 writes the unit to lib/systemd/system; on the merged-usr layout
# trixie uses, that is usr/lib/systemd/system, the same directory through a
# symlink, and systemd resolves the unit there. Delete this override once the
# cargo-deb pin moves to a release that writes the usr path.
dexd: aliased-location

# The tag asks the changelog to close an intent-to-package bug, a rule for
# packages uploaded into the Debian archive. The dexd package is built in CI and
# installed on the project's own devices.
dexd: initial-upload-closes-no-bugs

# Lintian matches the string `did not find expected <stream-start>`, one of
# libyaml's error messages, which yaml-rust2 reproduces because it is a Rust port
# of libyaml's scanner and parser. The arm64 binary links no libyaml: `ldd` lists
# none, `strings` finds no libyaml C symbol, and no crate in that subtree has a
# build.rs, a `links` key or a `-sys` name. Re-check the override if the YAML
# dependency is ever swapped for one with a C backend.
dexd: embedded-library libyaml [usr/bin/dexd]
dexd: embedded-library libyaml [usr/bin/dex-exhibit-apply]
